{"tfa": {"type": "standard", "title": "Valley_Parade", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Valley Parade</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "wikibase_item": "Q969279", "titles": {"canonical": "Valley_Parade", "normalized": "Valley Parade", "display": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Valley Parade</span></span>"}, "pageid": 599315, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T00:00:04Z", "description": "Football stadium in Bradford, West Yorkshire, England", "description_source": "local", "coordinates": {"lat": 53.80416667, "lon": -1.75888889}, "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Parade", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Parade?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Parade?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Valley_Parade"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Parade", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Valley_Parade", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Parade?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Valley_Parade"}}, "extract": "Valley Parade, currently known as Mbanq Valley Parade for sponsorship reasons, is an all-seater football stadium in Bradford, West Yorkshire, England. The stadium was built in 1886 as the home of Manningham Rugby Football Club; it remained so until 1903, when the club changed code from rugby league to association football, and became Bradford City A.F.C. Valley Parade has since been Bradford City's home ground, and is now owned by the pension fund of the club's former chairman Gordon Gibb. The stadium has also hosted Bradford for one season and the rugby-league side Bradford Bulls for two seasons, and has accommodated a number of England youth team fixtures. In 1908, the football architect Archibald Leitch was commissioned to redevelop the ground when Bradford City were promoted to the First Division.", "normalizedtitle": "Valley Parade"}, "mostread": {"date": "2026-09-26Z", "articles": [{"views": 421359, "rank": 4, "type": "standard", "title": "Lizzie_Borden", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lizzie Borden</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 214796, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Lizzie_Borden_1890.jpg/330px-Lizzie_Borden_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 386}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Lizzie_Borden_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 640, "height": 748}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T02:04:32Z", "description": "American woman acquitted of murder (1860\u20131927)", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie_Borden", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie_Borden?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie_Borden?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lizzie_Borden"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie_Borden", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Lizzie_Borden", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie_Borden?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lizzie_Borden"}}, "extract": "Lizzie Andrew Borden was an American woman who was tried and acquitted of the murders of her father and stepmother in Fall River, Massachusetts. No other individuals were charged with the murders.", "normalizedtitle": "Lizzie Borden"}, {"views": 376033, "rank": 5, "type": "standard", "title": "Ted_Kaczynski", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ted Kaczynski</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 18621887, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Ted_Kaczynski_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ted_Kaczynski_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 440}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Ted_Kaczynski_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 1031, "height": 1376}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T01:02:44Z", "description": "American domestic terrorist (1942\u20132023)", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Kaczynski", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Kaczynski?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Kaczynski?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ted_Kaczynski"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Kaczynski", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ted_Kaczynski", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Kaczynski?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ted_Kaczynski"}}, "extract": "Theodore John Kaczynski, also known as the Unabomber, was an American mathematician and domestic terrorist. A mathematics prodigy, he abandoned his academic career in 1969 to pursue a reclusive primitive lifestyle and lone wolf terrorism campaign.", "normalizedtitle": "Ted Kaczynski"}, {"views": 370335, "rank": 6, "type": "standard", "title": "Roblox", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Roblox</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 18514671, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T21:35:20Z", "description": "Multiplayer game creation platform", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roblox", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roblox?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roblox?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Roblox"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roblox", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Roblox", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roblox?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Roblox"}}, "extract": "Roblox is an online game platform and game creation system developed by Roblox Corporation that allows users to program and play games created by themselves or other users. It was developed by David Baszucki and Erik Cassel in 2004, and released to the public in 2006. As of February 2025, the platform has reported an average of 85.3\u00a0million daily active users. According to the company, its monthly player base includes half of all American children under the age of 16.", "normalizedtitle": "Roblox"}, {"views": 260257, "rank": 7, "type": "standard", "title": "India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">India at the 2026 Asian Games</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 82744644, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Flag_of_India.svg/330px-Flag_of_India.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 220}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Flag_of_India.svg/960px-Flag_of_India.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 900, "height": 600}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T04:14:47Z", "description": "Sporting event delegation", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:India_at_the_2026_Asian_Games"}}, "extract": "India is participating in the 2026 Asian Games in Aichi Prefecture, Japan from 19 September to 4 October 2026. This is the country's 20th consecutive appearance in the competition, having made its debut at the inaugural 1951 Asian Games. The Indian contingent consisted of 495 athletes competing in 36 sports. Shooter Manu Bhaker and men's kabaddi captain Pawan Sehrawat were the nation's flag-bearers during the opening ceremony.", "normalizedtitle": "India at the 2026 Asian Games"}, {"views": 259696, "rank": 8, "type": "standard", "title": "2026_Asian_Games_medal_table", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">2026 Asian Games medal table</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 82893793, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:57:04Z", "description": "Award", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:2026_Asian_Games_medal_table"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games_medal_table?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:2026_Asian_Games_medal_table"}}, "extract": "The 2026 Asian Games, officially known as the XX Asian Games or Aichi\u2013Nagoya 2026, is the largest sporting event in Asia governed by Olympic Council of Asia (OCA). They are currently being held from 19 September to 4 October 2026 in Aichi Prefecture and Nagoya, Japan, with 469 events in 43 sports and disciplines featured in the Games.", "normalizedtitle": "2026 Asian Games medal table"}, {"views": 229525, "rank": 9, "type": "standard", "title": "2026_Asian_Games", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">2026 Asian Games</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 51790406, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/2026_Asian_Games_logo.svg/330px-2026_Asian_Games_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 438}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/2026_Asian_Games_logo.svg/250px-2026_Asian_Games_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 193, "height": 256}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T00:31:46Z", "description": "Multi-sport event in Aichi and Nagoya, Japan", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:2026_Asian_Games"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/2026_Asian_Games", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Asian_Games?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:2026_Asian_Games"}}, "extract": "The 2026 Asian Games , officially the XX Asian Games (\u7b2c\u4e8c\u5341\u56de\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u7af6\u6280\u5927\u4f1a) and also known as Aichi\u2013Nagoya 2026 (\u611b\u77e5\u30fb\u540d\u53e4\u5c4b2026), is an ongoing multi-sport event being held in Aichi Prefecture in Japan from 19 September to 4 October 2026 though several competitions started from 10 September. Nagoya, capital city of Aichi Prefecture, is the third Japanese city to host the Asian Games, after Tokyo in 1958 and Hiroshima in 1994. Though Aichi Prefecture is the primary host, the competitions are taking place in three other prefectures and Tokyo Metropolis as well. The event has returned to its traditional four-year cycle, after the 2022 edition was postponed to 2023 due to the COVID-19 pandemic. The Games marked the 75th anniversary of the 1951 Asian Games held in New Delhi, India.", "normalizedtitle": "2026 Asian Games"}, {"views": 210483, "rank": 10, "type": "standard", "title": "The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)", "displaytitle": "<i>The Paradise</i> (2026 Indian film)", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 80682580, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bb/The_Paradise_%282026_Indian_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 258, "height": 387}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bb/The_Paradise_%282026_Indian_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 258, "height": 387}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:34:10Z", "description": "2026 Indian film by Srikanth Odela", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:The_Paradise_(2026_Indian_film)"}}, "extract": "The Paradise is a 2026 Indian Telugu-language period action drama film directed by Srikanth Odela and produced by Sudhakar Cherukuri and Ishan Saksena, under Sri Lakshmi Venkateshwara Cinemas and IVY Entertainment, respectively. The film stars Nani, Mohan Babu, Kayadu Lohar, Sonali Kulkarni and Raghav Juyal in the lead roles. In the film, Nani plays the leader of a struggling tribe in 1980s Secunderabad as they battle discrimination and fight for citizenship.", "normalizedtitle": "The Paradise (2026 Indian film)"}, {"views": 204136, "rank": 11, "type": "standard", "title": "Justin_Verlander", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Justin Verlander</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 3616702, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Justin_Verlander_in_2016.jpg/330px-Justin_Verlander_in_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 396}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Justin_Verlander_in_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 1631, "height": 1958}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:51:51Z", "description": "American baseball player (born 1983)", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Verlander", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Verlander?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Verlander?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Justin_Verlander"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Verlander", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Justin_Verlander", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Verlander?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Justin_Verlander"}}, "extract": "Justin Brooks Verlander is a former American professional baseball pitcher who played 21 seasons of Major League Baseball (MLB). He played for the Detroit Tigers, Houston Astros, New York Mets, and San Francisco Giants. A three-time Cy Young Award winner, an American League (AL) Most Valuable Player (MVP) Award recipient, and a two-time World Series champion, Verlander is considered one of the greatest pitchers in baseball history.", "normalizedtitle": "Justin Verlander"}, {"views": 159635, "rank": 13, "type": "standard", "title": "Primetime_(film)", "displaytitle": "<i>Primetime</i> (film)", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 79450412, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Primetime_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 259, "height": 384}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Primetime_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 259, "height": 384}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T21:25:10Z", "description": "2026 film by Lance Oppenheim", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_(film)", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_(film)?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_(film)?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Primetime_(film)"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_(film)", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Primetime_(film)", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_(film)?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Primetime_(film)"}}, "extract": "Primetime is a 2026 American psychological crime thriller film directed by Lance Oppenheim in his narrative feature film debut. Based on the 2007 Esquire article \"Tonight on Dateline This Man Will Die\" by Luke Dittrich, the film follows the production of the reality television series To Catch a Predator. Robert Pattinson stars as series host Chris Hansen, and also serves as a producer. Merritt Wever, Skyler Gisondo, and Phoebe Bridgers play supporting roles.", "normalizedtitle": "Primetime (film)"}, {"views": 131276, "rank": 14, "type": "standard", "title": "Christa_Pike", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Christa Pike</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 15838471, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T18:39:41Z", "description": "American convicted murderer (born 1976)", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christa_Pike", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christa_Pike?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christa_Pike?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Christa_Pike"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christa_Pike", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Christa_Pike", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christa_Pike?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Christa_Pike"}}, "extract": "Christa Gail Pike is an American convicted murderer who is incarcerated on death row in Tennessee. In 1995, when she was 18, Pike murdered her 19-year-old Job Corps classmate Colleen Slemmer in Knoxville. Pike and two friends led Slemmer into the woods, where they tortured and killed her. In 1996 Pike was sentenced to death, making her one of the youngest women to be sentenced to death in the United States during the post-Furman period. She is scheduled to be executed on September 30, 2026. If carried out, she will be the 19th woman executed nationwide since 1976 and the first woman executed in Tennessee in over 200 years. Pike's sentence remains controversial, as experts have opined that her legal defense failed to present mitigating evidence at trial, including the effect of her youth and childhood trauma on her decision-making abilities.", "normalizedtitle": "Christa Pike"}, {"views": 124353, "rank": 15, "type": "standard", "title": "Deaths_in_2026", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Deaths in 2026</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 81858235, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:29:55Z", "description": "", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_in_2026", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_in_2026?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_in_2026?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Deaths_in_2026"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_in_2026", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Deaths_in_2026", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_in_2026?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Deaths_in_2026"}}, "extract": "The following notable deaths occurred in 2026. Names are reported under the date of death, in alphabetical order. A typical entry reports information in the following sequence:Name, age, country of citizenship at birth, subsequent nationality, what subject was noted for, cause of death, and a reference.", "normalizedtitle": "Deaths in 2026"}, {"views": 119893, "rank": 16, "type": "standard", "title": "Aileen_Wuornos", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Aileen Wuornos</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "pageid": 214928, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/Aileen_Wuornos_%284x5_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 265, "height": 322}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/Aileen_Wuornos_%284x5_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 265, "height": 322}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:48:20Z", "description": "American serial killer (1956\u20132002)", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aileen_Wuornos", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aileen_Wuornos?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aileen_Wuornos?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Aileen_Wuornos"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aileen_Wuornos", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Aileen_Wuornos", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aileen_Wuornos?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Aileen_Wuornos"}}, "extract": "Aileen Carol Wuornos was an American serial killer. Between 1989 and 1990, while engaging in street prostitution along highways in Florida, Wuornos shot, killed, and robbed seven of her male clients. She initially claimed that her victims had either raped or attempted to rape her, and that the homicides were committed in self-defense, but later abandoned this defense. Wuornos was sentenced to death for six of the murders and was executed in 2002 after spending more than ten years on Florida's death row.", "normalizedtitle": "Aileen Wuornos"}]}, "image": {"title": "File:Gladiolus dalenii flower Ooty Jul25 A7CR 06187-224 zsp.jpg", "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Gladiolus_dalenii_flower_Ooty_Jul25_A7CR_06187-224_zsp.jpg/960px-Gla